# Keys only. Which providers run is chosen in src/agent/agent.tsx (<Agent llm stt tts>).
# A chosen provider whose key is missing fails with an error naming its variable; the
# table in node_modules/curb/docs/agent-guide/configuration.md lists every key. A new
# provider's key also goes into package.json curb.requiredRuntimeSecrets.
# Every curb command loads .env, and `npx curb secrets push` copies it to the hosted agent.

# KugelAudio runs the whole agent: its EU-hosted LLM thinks (kugelaudio.llm()), Kugel Ear
# listens (kugelaudio.stt()) and Kugel TTS speaks (kugelaudio.tts()). A hosted agent gets
# access from the platform.
# Locally, KugelAudio access comes from `npx curb login`: there is no key to copy.
# KUGELAUDIO_API_KEY=   # optional: an API key instead of npx curb login (CI, servers)

# Your own LiveKit, only for `npm start` (the self-hosted voice worker):
# LIVEKIT_URL=wss://your-project.livekit.cloud
# LIVEKIT_API_KEY=
# LIVEKIT_API_SECRET=
